From b4de9f12ff7a294fd1ad69269e83de00c94e87d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Primarosa <3505087+simonepri@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 23:22:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pkg/clickhouse: skip the column when decoding stored lines

The ClickHouse ingester stores interpreted frames, such as Python
frames from the agent, without their function names. The UI shows each
of them as 0x0. decodeLineInfo reads the line number and then takes the
next byte as the has-function flag, but every location encoder writes
the column number between the two, as DecodeSymbolizationInfo expects.
With a column of 0 the flag reads false and the function is skipped.

Skip the column before reading the flag. The new test encodes a location
with EncodeOtelLocation and checks that the function survives decoding
for several column values; it fails before the change.
---
 pkg/clickhouse/ingester.go      |  4 ++++
 pkg/clickhouse/ingester_test.go | 38 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 42 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 pkg/clickhouse/ingester_test.go

diff --git a/pkg/clickhouse/ingester.go b/pkg/clickhouse/ingester.go
index 128a1a29..4e1f5240 100644
--- a/pkg/clickhouse/ingester.go
+++ b/pkg/clickhouse/ingester.go
@@ -211,6 +211,10 @@ func decodeLineInfo(data []byte) LineInfo {
 		offset += n
 		info.LineNumber = int64(lineNum)
 
+		// Skip column, which every location encoder writes after the line number.
+		_, n = varint.Uvarint(data[offset:])
+		offset += n
+
 		hasFunction := data[offset] == 0x1
 		offset++
 
diff --git a/pkg/clickhouse/ingester_test.go b/pkg/clickhouse/ingester_test.go
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..d884ab65
--- /dev/null
+++ b/pkg/clickhouse/ingester_test.go
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
